                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                <div id=""mdbook-content"" class=""content"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                    <main>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                        <h1 id=""web-dashboard-and-json-api""><a class=""header"
                  & """ href=""#web-dashboard-and-json-api"">Web dashboard and JSON API</a></h1>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>adacovex --target=. --serve --port=8080</code> runs the full assess"
                  & "ment and then"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "starts a built-in HTTP/1.1 server (no external web stack) that serves a"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<strong>viewable HTML dashboard</strong> plus a machine-readable JSON API an"
                  & "d the SVG"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "badges. The server blocks until interrupted "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " run it in its own terminal, or"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "as a background process when scripting.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">adacovex --target=. --serve --port=8080"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "# in another terminal:"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "curl http://localhost:8080/api/metrics"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</code></pre>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""how-to-use-the-dashboard""><a class=""header"" href=""#how-to-use-the-da"
                  & "shboard"">How to use the dashboard</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> in a browser. The page is a singl"
                  & "e self-contained"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "document (no external assets) with hash-routed tabs. Use the header dropdown"
                  & " to"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "switch themes (light / dark / system) and <strong>Save settings</strong> to "
                  & "persist your"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "choice.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""overview-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#overview-tab"">Overview tab</a"
                  & "></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Overview tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><sp"
                  & "an class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Overview tab -- see the online manual "
                  & "for the image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Start here. The <strong>Robustness tier</strong> (S / A / B / C / D) is a"
                  & " single letter that"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "summarises five quality axes: Docs, Proof, Tests, Compliance, and Deps. An <"
                  & "strong>S</strong>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "means the project is healthy across the board. A <strong>D</strong> means on"
                  & "e or more axes"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "are below 50%. Below that:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>SPARK radar</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " proved verification conditions per check category (flow,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "initialization, runtime, assertions, functional). A balanced polygon means"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "every category has strong coverage. A spike in one corner and a flat line in"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "another means the proof effort is uneven.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Tests donut</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " passed vs failed tests. A full green arc means 100%"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "passing. Any red slice means the test suite has failures that must be fixed"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "before the project can be assessed as <code>Achieved</code>.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Doc coverage donut</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " documented subprograms as a percentage of"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "total. Strict mode requires 100%. A shortfall here shows exactly how many"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "subprograms are missing <code>--</code> docstrings.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Dependency scope ring</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " the resolved graph broken down by scope"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(base / dev / transitive / vendored / system / test).  It sits in the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "same row as the doc-coverage donut so the Overview uses its width well."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Each coloured segment is hoverable: hovering shows the scope name and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "its component count (for example <code>test: 3</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Proof check bars scale with the category"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s magnitude, the same way as the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "test-category bars: a 407-VC category reads as a longer bar than a 56-VC"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "one, so relative proof effort is visible at a glance.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""proof-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-tab"">Proof tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Proof tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><span "
                  & "class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Proof tab -- see the online manual for th"
                  & "e image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Shows the SPARK level (Stone .. Platinum) and per-category VC counts. The"
                  & " mini <strong>VCs proved / total</strong> at the top is the headline number."
                  & " Click into a category to see the breakdown.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>If a category is low, that is where the proof effort must focus.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""tests-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#tests-tab"">Tests tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Tests tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><span "
                  & "class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Tests tab -- see the online manual for th"
                  & "e image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Every test category with its count and Pass / Fail. A single failing cate"
                  & "gory"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "is enough to fail the compliance gate (<code>Tests passing</code> must be <c"
                  & "ode>Yes</code> for every"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "tier except QM / DAL-E).</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""compliance-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#compliance-tab"">Compliance "
                  & "tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Compliance tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><"
                  & "span class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Compliance tab -- see the online man"
                  & "ual for the image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Shows the target integrity level, overall <code>Achieved</code> / <code>U"
                  & "nmet</code>, HLRs traced,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "orphan-tag state, and every unmet criterion. Use this to verify that every H"
                  & "LR"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "is tagged in source and that no tags are orphaned (tagged but not defined in"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>HLR.md</code>).</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""dependencies-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#dependencies-tab"">Depende"
                  & "ncies tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Dependencies tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em"
                  & "><span class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Dependencies tab -- see the online"
                  & " manual for the image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>An interactive dependency tree (or diagram) of every component in the gra"
                  & "ph. Use the filter input and scope checkboxes to focus on base, dev, transit"
                  & "ive, vendored, or system dependencies. Click a node to see its licence, PURL"
                  & ", parent, and a registry link. Use this tab to audit your supply chain: conf"
                  & "irm every vendored licence is compatible, see which system tools the build n"
                  & "eeds (the <code>system</code> scope), and trace each component back to its s"
                  & "ource.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The diagram view (toggle <strong>Tree / Diagram</strong>) renders the sam"
                  & "e graph as a directed diagram.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""charts-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#charts-tab"">Charts tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of Charts tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><span"
                  & " class=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of Charts tab -- see the online manual for "
                  & "the image.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Eight CSS-only cards show the same data as the Overview tab in a differen"
                  & "t"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "format: the two shared radars (Robustness and SPARK Proof by Check Type),"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "proof and test donuts, proof and test bar charts, the docstring radial"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "gauge, and the dependency scope polar ring. Use this to compare SPARK"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "proof, test results, doc coverage, and dependency scope at a glance. See"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<a href=""#metrics-charts"">Metrics charts</a> for the full card-by-card break"
                  & "down.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""api-tab""><a class=""header"" href=""#api-tab"">API tab</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><label class=""checkbox-label""><input class=""checkbox-img"" type=""checkbox"""
                  & "><em>Preview of API tab -- see the online manual for the image.</em><span cl"
                  & "ass=""img-wrapper""><em>Preview of API tab -- see the online manual for the im"
                  & "age.</em></span></label></p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>An interactive REST API playground: every endpoint the server dispatches "
                  & "on"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "as a searchable, clickable button, with a pretty-printed, syntax-highlighted"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "JSON preview. The first endpoint (<code>/api/metrics</code>) runs automatica"
                  & "lly, so"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the tab opens with a live preview. See <a href=""#api-playground"">API playgro"
                  & "und</a>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "for the full detail.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""interpreting-the-charts""><a class=""header"" href=""#interpreting-the-c"
                  & "harts"">Interpreting the charts</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Green / full arcs</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " the metric is at 100% or close to it.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Red slices or flat corners</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " there is a regression or missing data.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Scope rings</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " a large vendored wedge means strict-mode docstrings are"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "being suppressed by patches. If you see no wedge, vendored code can be"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "uncovered.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Tier letter drops</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " a drop from <code>A</code> to <code>C</code> means the average across all"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "five axes fell. Check the axis table to see which one regressed.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The same data is available headlessly at <code>/api/metrics</code> and vi"
                  & "a"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code> (<code>{""metrics"":..., ""dependencies"":...}<"
                  & "/code>).</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Path</th><th>Content</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /</code></td><td>HTML dashboard (tabbed)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/metrics</code></td><td>JSON object with the key asses"
                  & "sment metrics</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/deps</code></td><td>JSON dependency graph (same data "
                  & "as the Dependencies tab)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /api/endpoints</code></td><td>JSON endpoint catalog (the l"
                  & "ist the API playground builds its UI from)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /docs</code></td><td>The bundled offline manual: the mdBoo"
                  & "k manual built into the binary (HTML, no external assets)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/spark.svg</code></td><td>SPARK assurance level badg"
                  & "e</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/tests.svg</code></td><td>Test pass/fail badge</td><"
                  & "/tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/do178c.svg</code></td><td>DO-178C compliance badge "
                  & "(Achieved / Unmet)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/iso26262.svg</code></td><td>ISO 26262 compliance ba"
                  & "dge</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>GET /badge/iec62304.svg</code></td><td>IEC 62304 compliance ba"
                  & "dge</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>anything else</td><td><code>404 Not Found</code></td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The server runs a small HTTP/1.1 implementation with a 4-worker task pool"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(configurable with <code>--serve-workers=N</code>, which is a related flag o"
                  & "f"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>--serve</code>) and serves requests until the process is interrupted ("
                  & "Ctrl-C)."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Query strings and URL fragments are stripped before routing, so"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>/?theme=light</code>, <code>/api/metrics?x=1</code> and <code>/api/dep"
                  & "s#top</code> reach the same"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "handlers as <code>/</code>, <code>/api/metrics</code> and <code>/api/deps</c"
                  & "ode> instead of 404ing.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""bundled-offline-manual""><a class=""header"" href=""#bundled-offline-man"
                  & "ual"">Bundled offline manual</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The <code>--serve</code> server also serves the <strong>bundled offline m"
                  & "anual</strong> at <code>/docs</code>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(both spellings, with and without the trailing slash, reach the same page)."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "The manual is the same Markdown source that powers the Read the Docs site"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(<code>docs/</code>, an mdBook project with <code>book.toml</code> and <code"
                  & ">SUMMARY.md</code>); at build"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "time <code>tools/gen-docs.py</code> runs <code>mdbook build</code> and inlin"
                  & "es the resulting"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>print.html</code> into the binary (<code>src/adacovex-docs_template.ad"
                  & "s</code>), so the page"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "is fully self-contained: stylesheets are inlined, external fonts and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "interactive scripts are dropped, and the HTML stays pure ASCII.  Users on a"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "machine without a network connection can still open the manual from the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "dashboard "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " the footer <strong>Manual</strong> link and the API playground"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>/docs</code> endpoint both point at it.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""the-html-dashboard""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-html-dashboard"">The"
                  & " HTML dashboard</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The page is a single self-contained document (no external assets), bundle"
                  & "d"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "into the binary from <strong>modular resources</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <code>resources/dashboard.html</code> is"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "just the page skeleton. Author styles and scripts are split into focused"
