                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <em>polar ring</em> of base / dev / transitive /"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "vendored / system / test components (conic-gradient + CSS hole,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>--scope-*</code> theme variables) with a legend. Skipped when the grap"
                  & "h is"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "empty.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Each card is a different type (radar / radar / donut / bars / bars / radi"
                  & "al / donut / polar) so the tab reads at a glance without duplicating a data "
                  & "story. The two radars are shared with the Overview, so the Charts tab contai"
                  & "ns every Overview chart. No JavaScript is required for the charts (pure CSS/"
                  & "SVG). The radial gauge, the scope ring, and the radars follow the light/dark"
                  & " theme automatically via CSS variables.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The surrounding grid (<code>chart-grid</code>) is responsive and the page"
                  & " container is <code>max-width:1180px</code> so large monitors do not stretch"
                  & " cards. Rings are used where a part-to-whole distribution is the point. Bars"
                  & " are used where a max-normalised comparison across categories is the point.<"
                  & "/p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h3 id=""robustness-tier""><a class=""header"" href=""#robustness-tier"">Robustnes"
                  & "s tier</a></h3>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The Overview tab leads with a <strong>Robustness</strong> radar spider an"
                  & "d a tier rating"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(S / A / B / C / D) so the health of the whole project can be read at a"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "glance.  Five quality axes, each a <code>0..100</code> percentage:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Axis</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><strong>Docs</strong></td><td>Docstring coverage: documented subprog"
                  & "rams / total</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><strong>Proof</strong></td><td>SPARK VCs proved / total</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><strong>Tests</strong></td><td>Test pass rate: passed / (passed + fa"
                  & "iled)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><strong>Comp</strong></td><td>Compliance gate: <code>100</code> when"
                  & " the target standard is Achieved, <code>0</code> when Unmet</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><strong>Deps</strong></td><td>Dependency hygiene: (graph components "
                  & "- vendored) / total</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The average of the five axes maps to the tier letter:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Tier</th><th>Average</th><th>Colour</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>S</td><td>&gt;= 90</td><td>green</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>A</td><td>&gt;= 80</td><td>blue</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>B</td><td>&gt;= 65</td><td>purple</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>C</td><td>&gt;= 50</td><td>orange</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td>D</td><td>&lt; 50</td><td>red</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The radar polygon, the per-axis legend with percentages, and the tier chi"
                  & "p"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "are rendered as inline SVG/CSS with integer math (no floating point in the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "renderer) and use <code>var(--accent)</code> plus per-tier CSS variables, so"
                  & " they follow"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the light/dark theme.  Next to it, a small <strong>SPARK radar</strong> show"
                  & "s the proved"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "count per check type, also as an inline-SVG spider, and the <strong>Tests</s"
                  & "trong> donut"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "and <strong>Doc Coverage</strong> radial gauge give the same pass/fail and c"
                  & "overage"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "numbers as the full-size charts.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""standard-awareness""><a class=""header"" href=""#standard-awareness"">Sta"
                  & "ndard-awareness</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Like the <code>sbom</code> subcommand, the dashboard <strong>defaults to "
                  & "all standards</strong> when"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "no <code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code> / <code>--class</code> flag"
                  & " is given. The status badges and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the compliance card list every standard"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s label at the shared tier (DAL-C,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "ASIL B, Class A). An explicit standard flag narrows the dashboard to that"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "single standard (for example <code>--asil=B</code> shows only ISO 26262 at A"
                  & "SIL B). See"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<a href=""standards.html"">Standards</a> for the cross-standard tier mapping.<"
                  & "/p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""the-json-api""><a class=""header"" href=""#the-json-api"">The JSON API</a"
                  & "></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>/api/metrics</code> is a plain HTTP GET, so scripts and CI can cons"
                  & "ume the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "assessment without parsing HTML:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<pre><code class=""language-json"">{""spark_level"":""Platinum"",""total_vcs"":725,"""
                  & "proved_vcs"":725,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & " ""tests_passed"":1173,""tests_failed"":0,""doc_coverage"":100,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & " ""standard"":""all"",""level"":""DAL-C"",""dal_status"":""Achieved"","
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & " ""standards"":{""DO-178C"":{""level"":""DAL-C"",""status"":""Achieved""},"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "               ""ISO 26262"":{""level"":""ASIL B"",""status"":""Achieved""},"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "               ""IEC 62304"":{""level"":""Class A"",""status"":""Achieved""}}}"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</code></pre>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>spark_level</code></td><td>Assessed SPARK level (<code>Stone</"
                  & "code>..<code>Platinum</code>)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>total_vcs</code> / <code>proved_vcs</code></td><td>GNATprove v"
                  & "erification-condition counts</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>tests_passed</code> / <code>tests_failed</code></td><td>Test-r"
                  & "esult counts</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>doc_coverage</code></td><td>Docstring coverage, 0-100</td></tr"
                  & ">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>standard</code></td><td><code>do178c</code> | <code>iso26262</"
                  & "code> | <code>iec62304</code> | <code>all</code></td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>level</code></td><td>Level label for the top-level target (<co"
                  & "de>DAL-C</code>, <code>ASIL B</code>, "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(166)
                  & ")</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>dal_status</code></td><td><code>Achieved</code> or <code>Unmet"
                  & "</code></td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>standards</code></td><td>Per-standard <code>level</code> / <co"
                  & "de>status</code> object (present when <code>standard</code> is <code>all</co"
                  & "de>)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>/api/deps</code> serves the resolved dependency graph as JSON (the "
                  & "same data the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "SBOM embeds, minus the SBOM envelope):</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<pre><code class=""language-json"">[{""name"":""gnat_arm_elf"",""version"":""13.2.1"","
                  & """scope"":""dev"","
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "  ""parent"":""adacovex"",""kind"":""dependency"",""purl"":""pkg:generic/gnat_arm_elf@1"
                  & "3.2.1"","
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "  ""lang"":"""",""website"":"""",""description"":""System tool referenced by the projec"
                  & "t (dev dependency)""},"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & " ...]"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</code></pre>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>name</code> / <code>version</code></td><td>Component name and "
                  & "version</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td><code>base</code> | <code>dev</code> | <c"
                  & "ode>transitive</code> | <code>vendored</code> | <code>system</code> (a syste"
                  & "m tool is a <code>system</code>-scope dependency with a <code>pkg:generic/*<"
                  & "/code> PURL)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>parent</code></td><td>Parent component name (<code>(root)</cod"
                  & "e> for the root, or the index as <code>0</code>)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>kind</code></td><td><code>root</code> or <code>dependency</cod"
                  & "e></td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>purl</code></td><td>Package URL when derivable</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>lang</code></td><td>Primary language when known</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>website</code></td><td>Resolved source URL when known</td></tr"
                  & ">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>Short description (for example a sy"
                  & "stem-tool note) when present</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>On-disk, the same export is available via <code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code"
                  & ">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(<code>{""metrics"": {...}, ""dependencies"": [...]}</code> after any assessment"
                  & ").</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""api-playground""><a class=""header"" href=""#api-playground"">API playgro"
                  & "und</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The <strong>API</strong> tab turns the dashboard into a small interactive"
                  & " REST client."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Every route the server dispatches on is listed as a clickable button,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "grouped by purpose:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Metrics</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <code>GET /api/metrics</code> (JSON).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Dependencies</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <code>GET /api/deps</code> (JSON).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Badges</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " each <code>GET /badge/*.svg</code> endpoint (SVG).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Documentation</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <code>GET /docs</code>, the bundled offline manual (HTML).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>API</strong> "
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(147)
                  & " <code>GET /api/endpoints</code>, the endpoint catalog the playground is"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "built from.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>A filter input searches the endpoints as you type (matching path, purpose"
                  & ","
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "and group name), so you can jump straight to <code>metrics</code> or <code>b"
                  & "adge</code>. Clicking"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "an endpoint issues a live <code>fetch</code> against the serving origin and "
                  & "previews"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the response:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>JSON endpoints are pretty-printed (two-space indent) and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<strong>syntax-highlighted</strong> with the vendored <a href=""https://githu"
                  & "b.com/petersolopov/yace"">yace</a>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "tokenizer (<code>window.YaceTok</code>). A JSON-key rule colours object keys"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "separately from string values, so the payload reads like an IDE view."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Endpoint paths that appear inside the JSON payload (for example the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>/api/...</code> and <code>/badge/...</code> values in <code>/api/endpo"
                  & "ints</code>) become clickable"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "links to the live endpoints, and every endpoint button"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s path is itself a"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "link that opens the raw URL in a new tab.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>SVG badge endpoints show the live image above the raw markup.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>The <code>/docs</code> endpoint shows the bundled offline manual (the sa"
                  & "me page the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "footer <strong>Manual</strong> link opens).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>A toolbar on the result offers <strong>Copy</strong> (clipboard) and <str"
                  & "ong>Download</strong> (saves"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the raw response body to a file) for the JSON API response, so the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "playground doubles as a lightweight HTTP client without leaving the browser."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "The first endpoint (<code>/api/metrics</code>) runs automatically so the tab"
                  & " always"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "opens with a live preview. The endpoint list is <strong>not hardcoded</stron"
                  & "g> in client"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "JavaScript: the playground fetches it from <code>GET /api/endpoints</code>, "
                  & "the single"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "source of truth the server declares. Each request is made live against the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "instance, so what you preview is exactly what <code>curl</code> returns.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""themes""><a class=""header"" href=""#themes"">Themes</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The dashboard supports <strong>light</strong>, <strong>dark</strong>, and"
                  & " <strong>system</strong> themes. Colours are"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "driven by CSS custom properties, and a header dropdown switches live between"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "them. <strong>Save settings</strong> persists the current selection in <code"
                  & ">localStorage</code>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "(no cookies, key <code>adacovex-theme</code>).</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Theme resolution on page load:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ol>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>a <code>?theme=light|dark|system</code> query parameter on the dashboard"
                  & " URL."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "It always wins. This is the supported way to pin the theme when embedding"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the dashboard in an iframe. The server strips the query string before"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "routing, so <code>http://localhost:8080/?theme=light</code> (and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>?theme=dark</code> / <code>?theme=system</code>) serves the themed das"
                  & "hboard instead of"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "404ing.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>otherwise the explicit CLI theme (<code>--theme=light</code> / <code>--t"
                  & "heme=dark</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>otherwise the saved <code>localStorage</code> choice, if one was saved.<"
                  & "/li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>otherwise the system theme (<code>prefers-color-scheme</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ol>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>--theme</code> only sets the <em>initial</em> selection. The dropdo"
                  & "wn and Save settings"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "still override it afterwards in the browser.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""related-cli-flags""><a class=""header"" href=""#related-cli-flags"">Relat"
                  & "ed CLI flags</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><th>Flag</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</thead>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>--serve</code></td><td>off</td><td>Run the pipeline, then spaw"
                  & "n the HTTP dashboard server (blocking) on the port. It is a switch: passing "
                  & "<code>--serve</code> is the only way to start the server, and omitting it (t"
                  & "he default, <code>off</code>) renders and exits without serving. There is no"
                  & " <code>--no-serve</code>, because a flag already controls it</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>--port=N</code></td><td><code>8080</code></td><td>Server port "
                  & "(a valid <code>Positive</code> integer)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>--serve-workers=N</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td>HTTP s"
                  & "erver task-pool worker count for <code>--serve</code> (a valid <code>Positiv"
                  & "e</code> integer, capped at 256). Only relevant with <code>--serve</code></t"
                  & "d></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<tr><td><code>--theme=NAME</code></td><td><code>system</code></td><td>Initia"
                  & "l dashboard theme: <code>light</code> | <code>dark</code> | <code>system</co"
                  & "de> (case-insensitive)</td></tr>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</tbody>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</table>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</div>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & ""
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                    </main>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & ""
                  & ASCII.LF
