                  & "                <div id=""mdbook-content"" class=""content"">"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                    <main>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                        <h1 id=""ai--llm-usage-in-this-project""><a class=""hea"
                  & "der"" href=""#ai--llm-usage-in-this-project"">AI / LLM Usage in this Project</a"
                  & "></h1>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>This page collects everything about how AI tooling is used in the adacove"
                  & "x"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "project: the disclosure, why the code is trustworthy despite AI assistance, "
                  & "how"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "LLM agents are expected to work on the codebase, and the honest limits of"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "machine-generated code.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""ai-assistance-disclosure""><a class=""header"" href=""#ai-assistance-dis"
                  & "closure"">AI Assistance Disclosure</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>AI tools were used during development for boilerplate generation, contrac"
                  & "t drafting, and docstring formatting. This is stated plainly rather than hid"
                  & "den. The project"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s own dogfood target is a zero-dependency, fully documented, SPARK-proven Ad"
                  & "a codebase. AI-generated contributions must meet the same bar as hand-writte"
                  & "n ones.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>That bar is 100% docstring coverage, Platinum proof, zero justified VCs, "
                  & "and the full <code>make check</code> gate before they count.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""why-trust-this-code""><a class=""header"" href=""#why-trust-this-code"">W"
                  & "hy trust this code?</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Given the use of AI assistance, healthy skepticism is natural and encoura"
                  & "ged."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Reliability is grounded in proof and design, not implicit trust:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Formal Verification:</strong> core Ada logic is formally verifie"
                  & "d. It is Platinum"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "under <code>gnatprove</code> 16.1.0, 725 VCs, 0 unproved (see"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<a href=""proof/16.1.0-ledger.html"">docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</a>). The pro"
                  & "of is re-run by"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>make prove</code> on every change. It is a hard gate before any releas"
                  & "e.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Read-Only Engine:</strong> adacovex assesses input payloads, bui"
                  & "ld artifacts, and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "reports without modifying your source files in place. An AI-assisted tool th"
                  & "at"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "cannot write to the tree it audits is a smaller blast radius by design.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Open Auditability:</strong> fully open source under Apache-2.0. "
                  & "Every line, human"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "or AI-written, is inspectable.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<blockquote>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><em>Still skeptical?</em> See Ken Thompson"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s landmark paper,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<a href=""https://dl.acm.org/doi/epdf/10.1145/358198.358210""><em>Reflections "
                  & "on Trusting Trust</em></a>,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "on the fundamental nature of trust in software toolchains. The point is that"
                  & " no"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "software, compiler, or model is trustworthy purely by assertion. It must be"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "inspectable and independently verifiable.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</blockquote>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""how-llm-agents-work-on-this-codebase""><a class=""header"" href=""#how-l"
                  & "lm-agents-work-on-this-codebase"">How LLM agents work on this codebase</a></h"
                  & "2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><a href=""../AGENTS.html""><code>AGENTS.md</code></a> at the repo root is t"
                  & "he machine-readable project"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "brief. It carries the architecture tree, the pipeline, the SPARK discipline,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the Makefile targets, and the verification gates. An agent (or human) workin"
                  & "g"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "on the tree must read it first. It must follow it. In particular:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Match existing conventions</strong> and prefer editing existing "
                  & "files. Verify"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "non-trivial changes with the project"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s typecheck and tests.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Zero library dependency</strong> is a hard constraint. Use only "
                  & "the GNAT runtime."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "Keep <code>tools/*.py</code> pure-stdlib, <code>typing</code>-annotated Pyth"
                  & "on.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>SPARK proof discipline</strong> (enforced by <code>make prove</c"
                  & "ode> and the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>spark-off-check</code> gate): zero unproved VCs, zero justified VCs, n"
                  & "o"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>SPARK_Mode (Off)</code> outside the <code>Types.Implementation</code> "
                  & "and <code>Complexity</code>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "container packages (non-formal <code>Ada.Containers</code> are illegal in"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "SPARK_Mode-On code; see <code>docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>The quality gate is the contract.</strong> <code>make check</cod"
                  & "e> runs the same gates that"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "CI enforces before a release. A contribution that fails it is not done.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li><strong>Generated files are regenerated, not hand-edited.</strong> The v"
                  & "ersion constant,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "the dashboard template package, the architecture tree, the count-synced docs"
                  & ","
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "and the descriptions all come from <code>tools/*.py</code> scripts. Their <c"
                  & "ode>--check</code>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "modes verify they did not drift.</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The doc-sync tools (<code>tools/update-test-count.py</code> and <code>too"
                  & "ls/update-proof-status.py</code>) derive their file set from the tree itself"
                  & " (<code>tools/live_files.py</code>). They do not use a hardcoded list. A sta"
                  & "le metric cannot survive anywhere. Generated outputs and historical records "
                  & "(past-release changelogs, past proof ledgers) are excluded.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>They keep their release-time numbers.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""verifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
                  & "verifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them"">Verifying claims instead of trust"
                  & "ing them</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Every number in this repository"
                  & Character'Val(226)
                  & Character'Val(128)
                  & Character'Val(153)
                  & "s documentation is anchored to a generated"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "artifact, not to a human- or AI-written claim:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>VC counts and the SPARK level come from <code>obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.ou"
                  & "t</code> (via"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>make proof-status</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>Test counts come from <a href=""test_result.html"">docs/test_result.md</a>"
                  & " (via"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>make test-count</code>).</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<li>Crate descriptions come from <code>alire/description.txt</code> and"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>alire/long-description.txt</code> (via <code>make description</code>)."
                  & "</li>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</ul>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>The CI badge <code>docs/badges/*.svg</code> files are emitted by the asse"
                  & "ssment itself."
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "If a document carries a number that does not match the artifact, one of the"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<code>--check</code> gates in <code>make check</code> fails loudly. That is "
                  & "the point.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""working-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human""><a class=""header"" href=""#w"
                  & "orking-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human"">Working in a fork or branch (LLM or"
                  & " human)</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Because the gates are cheap and deterministic, the safest workflow is to"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "iterate locally and let <code>make check</code> be the arbiter:</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">make build &amp;&amp; make test      # nati"
                  & "ve suite must stay 738/738"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "make prove                   # Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "make check                   # full gate: static checks, build, test, prove,"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "                             # doc, sbom, then tree-wide count-sync checks"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "</code></pre>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>make check</code> runs the cheap static gates first (ascii, spark-o"
                  & "ff, changelog, version source, doc links). A formatting or sync problem fail"
                  & "s before the expensive build and SPARK proof. Then it verifies the count-syn"
                  & "c checks (<code>test-count --check</code>, <code>proof-status --check</code>"
                  & ", <code>description --check</code>). A stale metric anywhere in the tree fai"
                  & "ls loudly.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>Regenerated files that are byte-identical when nothing changed (the versi"
                  & "on constant, the dashboard template) are left untouched. <code>git status</c"
                  & "ode> stays quiet.</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<h2 id=""the-served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface""><a class=""header"" href=""#th"
                  & "e-served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface"">The served dashboard as a trust surfa"
                  & "ce</a></h2>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p><code>adacovex --serve</code> renders a live HTML dashboard at <code>/</c"
                  & "ode>. It also renders a JSON API at <code>/api/metrics</code> and SVG badges"
                  & " at <code>/badge/*.svg</code>. The same numbers that an agent or reviewer qu"
                  & "otes from the CLI are visible and machine-checkable in the browser. The dash"
                  & "board shell is a real file (<code>resources/dashboard.html</code>).</p>"
                  & ASCII.LF
                  & "<p>It is bundled at build time by <code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code>. Page "
